\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Schematic of the arc discharge and of the near-electrode regions. (a) The arc column, described by an LTE model of the bulk plasma, between the cathode and the anode; the dashed boxes mark the cathode and anode regions (thickness exaggerated) that the present model resolves along the axis, from the electrode surface, \(x=0\), to the bulk-plasma boundary, \(x=L\). (b) Cathode and (c) anode region, not to scale: the space-charge sheath, the quasi-neutral non-equilibrium layer and the near-LTE plasma, with qualitative electron and heavy-particle temperatures, the particle fluxes at the surface and the data imposed at the two ends of the domain (Section~\ref {sec:model-bc}). The radial loss of the column is included at the cathode only (Section~\ref {sec:model-governing}).}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{1}{3}{Schematic of the arc discharge and of the near-electrode regions. (a) The arc column, described by an LTE model of the bulk plasma, between the cathode and the anode; the dashed boxes mark the cathode and anode regions (thickness exaggerated) that the present model resolves along the axis, from the electrode surface, \(x=0\), to the bulk-plasma boundary, \(x=L\). (b) Cathode and (c) anode region, not to scale: the space-charge sheath, the quasi-neutral non-equilibrium layer and the near-LTE plasma, with qualitative electron and heavy-particle temperatures, the particle fluxes at the surface and the data imposed at the two ends of the domain (Section~\ref {sec:model-bc}). The radial loss of the column is included at the cathode only (Section~\ref {sec:model-governing})}{figure.1}{}}
