\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The sheaths at the cathode (left) and the anode (right). (a), (b) Electron and ion mean free paths, the length \(\lambda _{T_h}\) over which ions and atoms exchange energy, and the electron Debye length, from the local state; dotted: the distance \(x\) from the electrode. (c), (d) Electron density and the Boltzmann relation \(n_B=n_e(x_{\rm  s})\exp [(e/k_B)\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ _{\phi _{\rm  s}}^{\phi }d\phi '/T_e]\) started at the sheath edge, with the ion density for reference. (e), (f) Ion velocity towards the electrode, \(u_i=\Gamma _i/n_i\), relative to the Bohm velocity \(u_B=\sqrt  {k_B(T_e+T_h)/M}\). The vertical dashed line marks the sheath edge \(x_{\rm  s}\).}}{15}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:base-sheath}{{7}{15}{The sheaths at the cathode (left) and the anode (right). (a), (b) Electron and ion mean free paths, the length \(\lambda _{T_h}\) over which ions and atoms exchange energy, and the electron Debye length, from the local state; dotted: the distance \(x\) from the electrode. (c), (d) Electron density and the Boltzmann relation \(n_B=n_e(x_{\rm s})\exp [(e/k_B)\int _{\phi _{\rm s}}^{\phi }d\phi '/T_e]\) started at the sheath edge, with the ion density for reference. (e), (f) Ion velocity towards the electrode, \(u_i=\Gamma _i/n_i\), relative to the Bohm velocity \(u_B=\sqrt {k_B(T_e+T_h)/M}\). The vertical dashed line marks the sheath edge \(x_{\rm s}\)}{figure.7}{}}
